 Thompson Helen Pearson Benjamin Thompson Subscribe Download the October 2026 long read podcastCritical thinking is a skill that is under threat from the AI revolution in large language models. But all is not lost. Specialists in education and cognition have long been studying critical thinking, and some have useful tips on how to stay cognitively sharp in the age of AI. This is an audio version of our Feature: How to stay smart in the age of AI: the science of critical thinkingNever miss an episode. Subscribe to the Nature Podcast on Apple Podcasts, Spotify, YouTube Music or your favourite podcast app. An RSS feed for the Nature Podcast is available too. doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-03228-3 Related Articles How to stay smart in the age of AI: the science of critical thinking In praise of human teachers: universities must resist outsourcing everything to AI The AI revolution is running out of data. What can researchers do? Assessing students in the AI era Subjects Latest on: Machine learning Education Brain Three reasons why AI is not conscious and perhaps never will be Comment 19 OCT 26 PhD students who write dissertations with AI less likely to stay in academia News 16 OCT 26 ArXiv versus AI slop: will capping preprint submissions work? News 15 OCT 26 Lessons from Katrina: how to rebuild academia from the ground up Career Feature 19 OCT 26 Is AI eroding PhD students’ critical thinking and analysis skills? Career News 15 OCT 26 Keep medical doctors in academia — without them, health-care research will suffer Comment 12 OCT 26 Microdosing LSD shows some cognitive benefits — but only for women News 19 OCT 26 Memory stays strong in old age when this brain enzyme is active News 16 OCT 26 Can GLP-1s heal the brain? Obesity drugs get a makeover for addiction and depression News 13 OCT 26","fetched_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:56.389Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<li data-test=\"article-category\"><span>NATURE PODCAST</span></li>","sentences":[{"en":"NATURE PODCAS